

1. First user needs to create an Application
	1. ClientID.
	2. Client Secret.
	3. Auth Code
	
	
in order to perform Auth2.0  follow below steps
1. User to create an account in Github repo
2. should have 1-2 repo in the account to get response.
3. User create an application in github
4. goto github profile > setting > developer setting on left
5. Click on OAuth apps on left side
6. Create an application >  New OAuth app
		a. Provide Application Name - SA2506029_API
		b. Home page URL - this could be any URL - https://www.facebook.com/
		c. Application description (Optional)
		d. Authorization Call back URL - https://www.facebook.com/
		e. Click on Register application button.
		f. application created successfully.
7. Generate Client ID and Client Secret
		a. Client ID will be there on page (copy and backup)
		b. Click on  "Generate a new client secret button"	 to generate client secret
		c. most important --> require to copy that client secret and backup
		d. click on update Application button (mandatory)

8. to get AuthCode, below URL to be hit over browser.
	URL ---> https://github.com/login/oauth/authorize?client_id=Ov23liyug4x21QB1n8Ar
9. User required to authorized above request to get AuthCode, user redirected to URL and that one would have auth code.

10. step to get Auth2.0
	a. Open Postman
	b. hit post request in postman - https://github.com/login/oauth/access_token?client_id=asdadsdadada21312313231&client_secret=123456789trewdfgh&code=1234567890876543
	c. please use client_id, client_secret_auth_code respective to the application.
	d. as output of step b --> recevied OAuth2.0 token (copy and backup)
11. get github data as reposnce using Auth2.0 token in get request.
		a. hit get request in Postman -> https://api.github.com/user/repos	
		b. supply bearer Token under Authorization tab
		c. user should get response as github repo detail.
		 	
	
	
	